      "message": "Stop charging twice for the space above a page\n\nEvery repository page paid for its top gap twice. `.cols` pads the\ncontent area by 22px, and then `.sec.top` - which exists to be the\nfirst section on a page - added 22px of its own. Forty-four pixels\nbefore any page's first line, on Code, Changes, Community, Review,\nCoverage and the rest. The first section keeps no margin now; the\nlayout's padding was always the right amount.\n\nTwo pages also said their own name twice. The tab bar names the page\nand marks it, and then the body opened with a heading repeating it:\nChanges under Changes, Community under Community. Both headings are\ngone, and with them a whole row each - the count and the controls that\nshared that row moved onto the row of filters underneath, which had\nspace for them.\n\nChange-Id: I3e9a5c17b0d4826fae13975cb2048d6e7a5f1c92\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
